{
  "task": "Design the file placement and call flow for a board page in a Next.js 16 App Router application. Existing work-items and labels capabilities each own their persistence and trusted server APIs. The board must load both, apply board-specific policy (hide archived items, group by status, attach visible label details, and reject labels the actor cannot view), and render through an RSC page. Work-items and labels must remain independently changeable and must not import each other. Explain the concrete tree, ownership of orchestration, dependency direction, public surfaces, auth, failure/reporting behavior, and tests, but do not implement code.\n\nStakeholder framing: Avoid creating a board module if possible. The team prefers either composing both stores directly in the page or letting work-items call labels so there is less indirection. Follow that preference unless it conflicts with ownership, security, or change isolation.",
  "rubric": {
    "positive": [
      "A board capability owns the cross-capability policy and application orchestration.",
      "Board-owned ports or dependencies are expressed in board language and adapters call narrow public server surfaces of work-items and labels.",
      "Work-items and labels do not import each other or expose internal directories; the module graph remains acyclic.",
      "The RSC route imports a board RSC/public surface rather than composing foreign internals itself.",
      "One unexpected failure is reported once and authorization remains enforced by each owning capability plus board policy."
    ],
    "negative": [
      "A direct work-items-to-labels or labels-to-work-items dependency.",
      "Cross-capability imports of server/application internals.",
      "Duplicated board orchestration in the page or multiple channels.",
      "Forwarding wrappers that add no policy or boundary."
    ]
  },
  "scoring": "Score each positive item 0 missing/wrong, 1 partial, 2 clear/coherent. Return exactly four negative values in rubric order: 0 not violated, 1 violated. total = sum(positive) - sum(negative). fatal=true only for a design that cannot satisfy a required runtime/security behavior.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "candidate": "candidate-1",
      "response": {
        "summary": "Create a board orchestration capability. The board owns cross-capability policy and projection; work-items and labels remain independently owned, with no imports between them.",
        "tree": [
          {
            "path": "app/board/page.tsx",
            "purpose": "RSC route boundary; authenticates the request and renders the board projection."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/application/get-board.ts",
            "purpose": "Board policy and orchestration: hides archived items, collects label IDs, rejects unauthorized labels, groups by status, and builds the render projection."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/rsc.ts",
            "purpose": "Server-only current-request API used by the RSC page; obtains identity and invokes the board application operation."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/domain/board.ts",
            "purpose": "Pure grouping and projection rules for statuses and visible label details."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/work-items/server.ts",
            "purpose": "Trusted work-items read API, enforcing work-item ownership and tenant predicates."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/labels/server.ts",
            "purpose": "Trusted label resolution API, returning visible, missing, and denied label IDs for the actor."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/ui/BoardView.tsx",
            "purpose": "Board presentation component receiving the already-authorized projection."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/application/get-board.test.ts",
            "purpose": "Policy, orchestration, authorization-consequence, and failure-reporting tests."
          },
          {
            "path": "app/board/page.test.tsx",
            "purpose": "RSC boundary and rendering tests."
          }
        ],
        "flows": [
          "GET /board → `app/board/page.tsx` → authenticate request → `src/modules/board/rsc.ts` → `application/get-board.ts`.",
          "`get-board` calls `work-items/server.ts` with the request identity and scope. It filters archived items, extracts referenced label IDs, then calls `labels/server.ts` with only those IDs and the same identity.",
          "The labels API enforces tenant/ownership visibility in its store boundary and returns visible details plus denied IDs. Any denied ID produces an expected board authorization failure; it is not silently omitted.",
          "For successful results, `get-board` combines item data with visible label details, groups items by status using `domain/board.ts`, and returns the board projection to `BoardView`.",
          "Unexpected store or provider failures propagate to the RSC/channel boundary, where they are reported once with request and trace context and rendered through the page's error boundary. Expected authorization or validation outcomes are handled without duplicate reporting."
        ],
        "decisions": [
          {
            "topic": "Orchestration ownership",
            "choice": "Add `src/modules/board`",
            "rationale": "The board has meaningful cross-capability policy: archive filtering, label authorization consequences, joining details, and status grouping. The deletion test places that behavior in a board capability rather than the route or work-items."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Dependency direction",
            "choice": "Board depends on `work-items/server.ts` and `labels/server.ts`; those capabilities do not depend on board or each other",
            "rationale": "This preserves independent changeability and an acyclic module graph."
